Only pass `-static-external` to a GHC that has it.

`executable-static: True` reaches Cabal as `withFullyStaticExe`, and the
stable-haskell Cabal fork turns that into GHC's `-static-external` (a
fork-only flag; see `docs/users_guide/phases.rst` in the GHC fork).
haskell.nix builds every v2 slice with this one cabal-install whatever
the compiler is, and `modules/cabal-project.nix` sets

    package *
      executable-static: True

for every musl host -- so a musl slice on a MAINLINE GHC gets a flag that
GHC does not know and the link dies before it starts:

    aarch64-unknown-linux-musl-ghc: unrecognised flag: -static-external
    Usage: For basic information, try the `--help' option.
    <no location info>: error:
        `cc' failed in phase `Linker'. (Exit code: 1)

(That is `x86_64-linux.unstable.ghc9124.aarch64-multiplatform-musl.tests.check-datadir.run-v2`
and every other musl v2 slice that links an executable.)

Ask the compiler instead of assuming.  The fork brands its `ghc --info`
with `("Edition","Stable Haskell")` and upstream emits no such field, so
that is the discriminator; haskell.nix already relies on it in
`lib/dummy-ghc.nix`, and `tests.dummy-ghc-info` keeps the two in step.

Compilers without the flag fall back to upstream Cabal's spelling of the
same request, `ghcOptLinkOptions = ["-static"]` (i.e. `-optl-static`) --
which is also what haskell.nix's v1 builder passes for musl, so the two
builders now agree on what `executable-static` means.

--- a/src/Distribution/Simple/GHC/Build/Link.hs	2026-08-24 12:42:38
+++ b/src/Distribution/Simple/GHC/Build/Link.hs	2026-08-24 12:42:52
@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@
 import Control.Monad
 import Control.Monad.IO.Class
 import qualified Data.ByteString.Lazy.Char8 as BS
+import qualified Data.Map as Map
 import qualified Data.Set as Set
 import Distribution.Backpack
 import Distribution.Compat.Binary (encode)
@@ -114,6 +115,16 @@
         | src <- extraSources
         ]
 
+      -- `-static-external` is a stable-haskell GHC flag; upstream GHC has no
+      -- such option and rejects the whole command line.  This Cabal is used
+      -- with both (haskell.nix builds every v2 slice with it, whatever the
+      -- compiler), so ask the compiler which spelling of `executable-static`
+      -- it understands.  The fork brands its `ghc --info` with `Edition`;
+      -- upstream emits no such field.
+      ghcHasStaticExternal =
+        Map.lookup "Edition" (compilerProperties (compiler lbi))
+          == Just "Stable Haskell"
+
       -- TODO: Shouldn't we use withStaticLib for libraries and something else
       -- for foreign libs in the three cases where we use `withFullyStaticExe` below?
       linkerOpts rpaths =
@@ -121,14 +132,21 @@
           { ghcOptExtraDefault =
               [ "-static-external"
               | withFullyStaticExe lbi
+              , ghcHasStaticExternal
               ]
           , ghcOptLinkOptions =
-              -- Pass extra `ld-options` given
-              -- through to GHC's linker.
-              maybe
-                []
-                programOverrideArgs
-                (lookupProgram ldProgram (withPrograms lbi))
+              -- Upstream's spelling of the same request, for compilers
+              -- without `-static-external`.
+              [ "-static"
+              | withFullyStaticExe lbi
+              , not ghcHasStaticExternal
+              ]
+                -- Pass extra `ld-options` given
+                -- through to GHC's linker.
+                ++ maybe
+                  []
+                  programOverrideArgs
+                  (lookupProgram ldProgram (withPrograms lbi))
           , ghcOptLinkLibs =
               if withFullyStaticExe lbi
                 then extraLibsStatic bi
